.TH L_GETIDENTITY 8 2026-11-17 Lustre "Lustre Configuration Utilities"
.SH NAME
l_getidentity \- Handle Lustre user/group cache upcall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY l_getidentity
.RB { -d | mdtname }
.I UID
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
The identity upcall command specifies the path to an executable that,
when properly installed, is invoked to resolve the numeric
.I UID
to a group membership list.
.PP
.B l_getidentity
is the reference implementation of the user/group cache upcall.
This command is normally run directly by the Lustre MDS service
and specifies the
.B mdtname
argument for the MDT that should be updated.
.SS "The permissions file"
.B /etc/lustre/perm.conf
supports a flat file database of permissions in the format:
.EX
.IB UID <space> NID <space> PERM1 , PERM2 ,..., PERMN
.EE
where
.I PERM
is one of:
.B [no]setuid
.B [no]setgid
.B [no]setgrp
.B [no]rmtacl
.B [no]rmtown
.PP
.BR nss (5)
modules can be enabled for auth handling by adding a
.B lookup
command with a list of nss modules to
.BR perm.conf .
Modules of several
.B lookup
lines are appended.
.PP
At the time of writing, known 
.BR nss (5)
modules include:
.BR lustre ", " nss_files ", " ldap ", " nis ", " sss ", and" systemd
additional modules may be documented in
.BR nsswitch.conf (5)
or installed separately.
.PP
.BR nss (5)
modules are searched in order. The user is taken from the first
module that knows the UID; supplementary groups are collected from
all modules. Supplementary groups come from the module's
.B initgroups_dyn
method, or from a scan of all group entries if the module has none.
.PP
A module name may be followed by options in brackets, separated by
commas, for example
.BR ldap[user] :
.TP
.B user
use the module for the user lookup only.
.TP
.B group
use the module for the supplementary group lookup only.
.TP
.B only
once the user is found in this module, take supplementary groups from
this module only. It has an effect only on a module that does both
user and group lookups, i.e. without
.B user
or
.B group
or with both; otherwise it is ignored.
.PP
A module without options does both lookups.
.PP
A special
.B lustre
module is used to enable lustre specific password and group
auth by way of
.B /etc/lustre/passwd
and
.B /etc/lustre/group
.PP
For historical reasons
.B nss_files
was needed to use the
.BR nss (5)
.B files
module.
This alias is now deprecated and will be removed in a future release.
.PP
Note for sites moving from
.BR l_getidentity_nss :
there the
.B files
module reads
.B /etc/lustre/passwd
and
.BR /etc/lustre/group ,
here it is the
.BR nss (5)
.B files
module (the system
.B /etc/passwd
and
.BR /etc/group ).
Replace
.B files
with
.B lustre
when moving a
.B perm.conf
from
.BR l_getidentity_nss .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -d
Run in debug mode and print supplementary groups information for
.I UID
to
.B stdout
instead of updating Lustre.
.SH FILES
.EX
.RI /{proc,sys}/fs/lustre/mdt/ mdt-service /identity_upcall
.RI /etc/lustre/perm.conf
.RI /etc/lustre/passwd
.RI /etc/lustre/group
.EE
.SH LIMITS
A maximum of 8 nss modules can be enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
The identity upcall command can be specified via:
.RS
.EX
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." MDTNAME .identity_upcall= PATH_TO_UPCALL
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable lustre auth and ldap:
.RS
.EX
[/etc/lustre/perm.conf]
.B # lookup lustre ldap
\&
[/etc/lustre/passwd]
root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash
\&...
[/etc/lustre/group]
root:x:0:root
\&...
.EE
.RE
Lustre passwd and group files use the same format as the system
.BR passwd (5)
and
.BR group (5)
files.
.P
In this configuration root is local to the cluster
and all other perms are delegated to ldap.
.PP
Look users up in ldap, then in the lustre files; take supplementary
groups from the lustre files only:
.RS
.EX
.B lookup ldap[user] lustre
.EE
.RE
.PP
Users known to the lustre files get groups only from them, others are
found in ldap and get groups from both modules:
.RS
.EX
.B lookup lustre[only] ldap
.EE
.RE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B l_getidentity
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 1.7.0
.\" Added in commit 1.6.0.1-152-gd2d56f38da
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR group (5),
.BR nss (5),
.BR passwd (5)
.PP
Lustre Programming Interfaces section of Lustre Operations Manual.
